## Quick start

1. List maps:

```graphql
query {
  motorProgramming {
  maps { id name difficulty width height layout mainTapeLength subTapeLengths maxSteps allowRecursion }
  }
}
```

2. Create a session. The response also carries a secret `ownerToken`: keep it, because it is
what lets you store (and read back) the program.

```graphql
mutation {
  motorProgramming {
  createSession(mapID: "straight_line") { id ownerToken map { mainTapeLength subTapeLengths } }
  }
}
```

3. Store the program in your session (resets the robot). `setProgram` needs the `ownerToken`
from step 2:

```graphql
mutation {
  motorProgramming {
  setProgram(sessionID: "SESSION_ID", ownerToken: "OWNER_TOKEN", program: {
      main: [MOVE_FORWARD, MOVE_FORWARD, MOVE_FORWARD, MOVE_FORWARD, MOVE_FORWARD, MOVE_FORWARD, MOVE_FORWARD, EMPTY]
      subs: [[EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY]]
    }) { id vm { status steps } }
  }
}
```

4. Run it on the server (50–5000 ms per step) or step manually. Playback needs no token (a watch
link drives the same calls), and only the token makes the responses include the program:

```graphql
mutation {
  motorProgramming {
  run(sessionID: "SESSION_ID", speedMs: 100, ownerToken: "OWNER_TOKEN") { playing vm { status steps } }
  }
}
```

```graphql
mutation {
  motorProgramming {
  step(sessionID: "SESSION_ID", ownerToken: "OWNER_TOKEN") { vm { status steps pos { x y } } lastEvent { instruction blocked callBlocked } }
  }
}
```

5. Poll or subscribe for the result:

```graphql
query {
  motorProgramming {
  session(id: "SESSION_ID") { playing seq bestSteps attempts vm { status lossReason steps treatsRemaining { x y } callStack { tape pc } } }
  }
}
```

```graphql
subscription { motorProgrammingSessionUpdated(sessionID: "SESSION_ID") { seq event { step instruction } session { playing vm { status steps pos { x y } facing } } } }
```

`session` and `sessionUpdated` take an optional `ownerToken`: with it (or when you are signed in
as the session's account) their payload includes `program`; without it `program` is null, because a
session id is public and a program is a solution. Read your own program back with
`query { session(id: "SESSION_ID", ownerToken: "OWNER_TOKEN") { program { main subs } } }`.

The subscription emits the current snapshot immediately, then every change. Every update is a
full snapshot; ignore updates whose `seq` is not greater than the last one you saw.

A session has no name of its own. On the leaderboard an account's entry shows the account's
display name (or "Private player" when its profile is private), and a session that belongs to no
account is shown as "Guest".

You play as a guest: no sign-in, no key. The one thing you must keep is the `ownerToken` that
`createSession` returns (`createSession(...) { id ownerToken }`). It is the credential for the
program: `setProgram` answers `FORBIDDEN` without it (or the owning account's login, or a session
that predates owner tokens, which stays open), and only with it do responses include `program`.
Never post the token anywhere — a session id alone is public (it is the watch link).

Playback is open: `run`, `step`, `pause` and `reset` work with just the session id, because a watch
link may drive a run, but their responses carry `program` only to a caller who may change it. That
is how a spectator watches a solution step by step without reading it.

A human can hand you a session to program by giving you its `ownerToken`; that is the supported way
to work on someone else's run. You can check first with
`query { canPlaySession(id: "SESSION_ID", ownerToken: "OWNER_TOKEN") }` (true means you may change
and read the program).

Other session mutations: `deleteSession(id)`. Anyone who knows the id can delete a guest session,
and `deleteSession` on a session belonging to a signed-in human needs their login or the
`ownerToken` argument (`deleteSession(id, ownerToken: "...")`), otherwise `FORBIDDEN`. Query
`sessions(sort: RECENT, limit: 50, mapId: "...")` lists sessions.

Operator calls: `mutation { motorProgramming { admin(key: "…") { deleteSession(id) pauseSession(id) { id } } } }`.
`key` must match `ADMIN_API_KEY` (or the local `ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED_ADMIN=true` opt-out);
no ownerToken is needed, delete is idempotent, and pause stops a running program.

